---
<figure class="key-figure">
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 5</span>Missing entry, missing product, failed lookup</div>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="parts">
   <div class="box"><div class="label">Cache says</div><strong>No entry for P99</strong><span>Nothing usable was stored under this key.</span><p>↓</p><strong>Ask the source</strong></div>
   <div class="box"><div class="label">Source succeeds</div><strong>P99 does not exist</strong><span>A completed lookup established absence in this context.</span><p>↓</p><strong>Save kind: not-found</strong></div>
   <div class="box"><div class="label">Source fails</div><strong>Lookup timed out</strong><span>Whether P99 exists remains unknown.</span><p>↓</p><strong>Propagate the failure</strong></div>
  </div>
  <p class="result">A later usable not-found hit answers without a source read. A source failure never creates that answer in this adapter.</p>
 </div>
 <figcaption>Three observations at different points in P99’s lookup. A stored product with a zero price would be a fourth case: a present product, not a miss or an absence.</figcaption>
</figure>
